# Termux Utilities - Cron Examples

# Copy and paste these into your crontab with: crontab -e

# =============================================================================
# SYSTEM SCRIPTS
# =============================================================================

# Run full system checks every hour
0 \* \* \* \* \~/termux-utilities/system/startup\_monitor.sh

# Run system checks with package updates daily at 3 AM
0 3 \* \* \* \~/termux-utilities/system/startup\_monitor.sh --update

# Monitor system metrics every 6 hours
0 \*/6 \* \* \* \~/termux-utilities/system/system\_monitor.sh

# Generate boot report at startup (requires Termux:Boot)
@reboot \~/termux-utilities/system/termux\_boot\_report.sh

# Check WiFi health every 30 minutes (only runs 8 AM - 11 PM)
\*/30 \* \* \* \* \~/termux-utilities/system/wifi\_health.sh

# =============================================================================
# BATTERY SCRIPTS
# =============================================================================

# Check battery every 15 minutes (alerts at 15%, 30%, 50%)
\*/15 \* \* \* \* \~/termux-utilities/battery/battery\_check.sh

# =============================================================================
# STORAGE SCRIPTS
# =============================================================================

# Clean logs older than 7 days every Sunday at 3 AM
0 3 \* \* 0 \~/termux-utilities/storage/clean\_logs.sh

# Delete APKs older than 30 days on the 1st of every month at 4 AM
0 4 1 \* \* \~/termux-utilities/storage/delete\_apk.sh

# Organize downloads daily at 2 AM
0 2 \* \* \* \~/termux-utilities/storage/organize\_downloads.sh

# =============================================================================
# WEATHER SCRIPTS
# =============================================================================

# Get weather updates daily at 7:30 AM
30 7 \* \* \* \~/termux-utilities/weather/weather\_notify.sh

# =============================================================================
# CUSTOMIZATION TIPS
# =============================================================================

# 1. To edit your crontab:
# crontab -e

# 2. To list your current cron jobs:
# crontab -l

# 3. To remove all cron jobs:
# crontab -r

# 4. Cron syntax:

# \* \* \* \* \* command
# │ │ │ │ │
# │ │ │ │ └── Day of week (0 - 6) (0 = Sunday)
# │ │ │ └──── Month (1 - 12)
# │ │ └────── Day of month (1 - 31)
# │ └──────── Hour (0 - 23)
# └────────── Minute (0 - 59)

# 5. Common schedules:
# @reboot       Run at startup
# @hourly       Run every hour
# @daily        Run once a day at midnight
# @weekly       Run once a week at midnight on Sunday
# \*/5 \* \* \* \*   Run every 5 minutes

# =============================================================================
# NOTES
# =============================================================================
# - All paths assume scripts are in \~/termux-utilities/
# - Adjust paths if you cloned the repo to a different location
# - Test scripts manually before adding to cron
# - Use absolute paths (starting with \~/) for reliability
# - Comments (lines starting with #) are ignored by cron
